authoring
setAnonymousWithUtilities
	"Private - Remember the current author identity and set an anonymous name during code
	 generation, using the legacy Squeak Utilities class API. A no-op when no Utilities class
	 is present or it does not support author initials. Legacy selectors are sent via perform:
	 behind a respondsTo: guard so no unimplemented selector is referenced directly."

	| authorClass |
	(Smalltalk hasClassNamed: #Utilities) ifFalse: [ ^ self ].
	authorClass := Smalltalk at: #Utilities.
	(authorClass respondsTo: #authorName)
		ifTrue: [ identity := authorClass perform: #authorName ].
	(authorClass respondsTo: #setAuthorInitials:)
		ifTrue: [ authorClass perform: #setAuthorInitials: with: self autogeneratedName ]